{"id":"s1.2.1","slug":"multiplying-by-11-trick","title":"Multiplying by 11 Trick","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">The 11's trick is a simplified version of the “moving down the line” multiplication method. To multiply a number by 11, you add consecutive digits of the number and record the result, keeping track of any carries.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For example, to calculate $523 \\times 11$:</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li><strong>Ones digit:</strong> 3</li><li><strong>Tens digit:</strong> 2 + 3 = 5</li><li><strong>Hundreds digit:</strong> 5 + 2 = 7</li><li><strong>Thousands digit:</strong> 5</li></ul><p>The result is <strong>5753</strong>. This trick can be extended to multiplication by 111, where you add triples of digits.</p>","summary":"The 11's trick is a simplified version of the “moving down the line” multiplication method.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem that involves multiplying a 2, 3, or 4-digit number by 11.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $11 \\times 54$.","answer":"594","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $11 \\times 72$.","answer":"792","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $11 \\times 38$.","answer":"418","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $462 \\times 11$.","answer":"5082","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $11 \\times 74$.","answer":"814","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $66 \\times 11$.","answer":"726","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $1.1 \\times 2.3$.","answer":"2.53","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $52 \\times 11$.","answer":"572","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":9,"text":"Calculate $246 \\times 11$.","answer":"2706","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":10,"text":"Calculate $111 \\times 456$.","answer":"50616","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":11,"text":"Calculate $198 \\div 11$.",